dpoint\", \"pass\": false}\n        ],\n        \"evidence_summary\": \"API is external-facing, PRD doesn't specify new signature\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"batch\": {\n    \"id\": \"202603161000\",\n    \"mode\": \"autopilot\",\n    \"parks_consecutive\": 0,\n    \"completed_prds\": [\n      {\n        \"filename\": \"00001-user-auth.md\",\n        \"cycles\": 2,\n        \"autonomous_decisions\": 3,\n        \"escalated_decisions\": 0,\n        \"tasks_completed\": 4,\n        \"tasks_total\": 4\n      }\n    ],\n    \"skips\": [\n      {\n        \"prd\": \"00110-flip-consensus-engine-default-v1.md\",\n        \"command\": \"test -f docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00110-evidence.md\",\n        \"exit_code\": 1,\n        \"note\": \"\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-03-16T10:03:41Z\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"catchup_completed_at\": \"2026-03-16T10:42:13Z\",\n    \"catchup_head_sha\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f6789...\"\n  },\n  \"doubts\": [],\n  \"doubts_rubric_verdicts\": [\n    {\"rule_id\": \"D1\", \"verdict\": \"pass\"},\n    {\"rule_id\": \"D2\", \"verdict\": \"pass\"},\n    {\"rule_id\": \"D3\", \"verdict\": \"pass\"},\n    {\"rule_id\": \"D4\", \"verdict\": \"fail\"},\n    {\"rule_id\": \"D5\", \"verdict\": \"pass\"}\n  ],\n  \"needs_attention\": false\n}\n```\n\n## Field Descriptions\n\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `prd` | string | PRD filename (with `.md` extension), e.g. `\"00004-feature-x.md\"`. Resolves to `docs/dev/project-management/prds/wip/<prd>` while active, or `docs/dev/project-management/prds/hold/<prd>` after a Phase 2 (`oversized_task`) or Phase 6 (`escalation_exhausted`) stall move. Phase 0's `subagent_prompt_overrun` replan handler does NOT move the PRD — it replans in place (PRD stays in `wip/`); a context-cap fire rotates (also in place, no move). Written by Phase 0 step 6 at PRD selection. The dashboard derives `name` by stripping the extension. |\n| `phase` | enum | Current gate: `build`, `review`, `done`, `paused`. `build` is ONE session (selection → catchup → design → planning → work, no mid-build handoff); the review surface runs in a fresh session; blind and doubt scrutiny are lenses inside every review cycle (PRD 00015), not phases. **Legacy values** `blind`/`doubt` (pre-00015 state files) map to the review gate on resume — `resume_target.py` sends them through one full review cycle. |\n| `next_phase` | string | Gate the next session of `/autopilot:run-autopilot` will run. Written by `/autopilot:run-autopilot` at every transition. **Read by the `autoclaude` wrapper after each headless session exits (PRD 00014)**: a non-empty gate (`build`/`review`/`done`) → relaunch a fresh session, and `\"\"` (empty, batch end) → archive state and stop the loop (drained). The authoritative resume signal is `phase` + `phases_completed`; build re-entry is by artifact (capsule freshness, tasks-exist, all-done). |\n| `prd_budget_since` | string? | ISO UTC timestamp marking the start of the current PRD's `_AUTOPILOT_PRD_BUDGET_USD` spend window. Stamped by `enter.py`'s `_write_prd` (step 10) when absent, or when the pre-write state's `prd` differs from the one being selected — so a PRD re-entry after a rotation or hand-off keeps its original stamp, and a genuinely new PRD selection gets a fresh one. Read by `cli/loop_decision.py` to total metrics-ledger spend since this timestamp against the budget; a total over budget parks the PRD (`park_site: \"budget\"`). Cleared by Phase 9 step 10 on PRD-to-PRD reset. |\n| `loop_entry` | object? | PRD 00282: the Phase 0 (`enter()`) result the loop ran in-process before launching a build session, or before consuming a `park-requested` marker — `Loop._pre_enter`. Shape: `{\"entered_by\": \"loop\", \"prd\": string, \"result\": object}`, where `result` is the same dict `autopilot enter` would otherwise print (its `warnings` key already popped and sent to the loop's own stderr). The session brief's `## Entry` section mirrors `result`'s `prd`/`catchup`/`design`/`stop`. The next `autopilot enter` call (inside the launched session) reads this FIRST: a `loop_entry.prd` matching `state.prd`, with no `--prd` given, replays `result` as that call's one JSON line and deletes `loop_entry` without re-run\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport tarfile\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\n\nimport pytest\nfrom buvis.pybase.result import FatalError\n\nfrom backup.capabilities.tar_archive import TarArchive\nfrom backup.config import BackupConfig\nfrom backup.runner import Runner\nfrom backup.step_result import PlanEntry\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from pathlib import Path\n\n    from pytest_mock import MockerFixture\n\n\ndef _config(tmp_path: Path, outputs: dict[str, str]) -> BackupConfig:\n    instances = {}\n    for name, out in outputs.items():\n        source = tmp_path / \"sources\" / name\n        source.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (source / \"tiny.txt\").write_bytes(name.encode())\n        instances[name] = {\"use\": \"tar-archive\", \"with\": {\"source\": str(source), \"out\": out}}\n    return BackupConfig.model_validate({\"instances\": instances})\n\n\ndef _assert_archive(out: Path, name: str) -> None:\n    with tarfile.open(out, \"r:gz\") as archive:\n        assert {member.name for member in archive.getmembers() if member.isfile()} == {f\"{name}/tiny.txt\"}\n        member = archive.extractfile(f\"{name}/tiny.txt\")\n        assert member is not None\n        assert member.read() == name.encode()\n\n\ndef _record_archive_creation(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> list[tarfile.TarFile]:\n    opened = []\n    real_open = tarfile.open\n\n    def record_open(*args: object, **kwargs: object) -> tarfile.TarFile:\n        archive = real_open(*args, **kwargs)\n        opened.append(archive)\n        return archive\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(tarfile, \"open\", record_open)\n    return opened\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"mode\", [\"run\", \"dry-run\", \"plan\"])\ndef test_runner_duplicate_groups_reject_all_members_and_keep_independent_outputs(\n    tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, mode: str\n) -> None:\n    shared = tmp_path / \"shared.tar.gz\"\n    second = tmp_path / \"second.tar.gz\"\n    shared.write_bytes(b\"keep first group\")\n    second.write_bytes(b\"keep second group\")\n    groups = {str(shared): [\"zinc\", \"alpha\", \"beta\", \"gamma\"], str(second): [\"omega\", \"delta\"]}\n    outputs = {name: out for out, names in groups.items() for name in names}\n    independent = {\n        \"shared-copy\": str(tmp_path / \"shared.tar.gz.copy\"),\n        \"prefix-shared\": str(tmp_path / \"prefix-shared.tar.gz\"),\n        \"other-directory\": str(tmp_path / \"nested\" / \"shared.tar.gz\"),\n    }\n    outputs.update(independent)\n    cfg = _config(tmp_path, outputs)\n    missing = tmp_path / \"sources\" / \"gamma\"\n    (missing / \"tiny.txt\").unlink()\n    missing.rmdir()\n    runner = Runner(cfg, dry_run=mode == \"dry-run\")\n    opened = _record_archive_creation(monkeypatch)\n    selected = list(cfg.instances.items())\n    results = runner.plan(selected) if mode == \"plan\" else list(runner.run(selected))\n    created = [[member.name for member in archive.members if member.isfile()] for archive in opened]\n    assert len(results) == len(outputs)\n    assert [result.label for result in results] == list(outputs)\n    assert created == ([[f\"{name}/tiny.txt\"] for name in independent] if mode == \"run\" else [])\n    for result in results:\n        if result.label in independent:\n            assert result.status == \"run\" if mode == \"plan\" else result.success is True\n            out = tmp_path / independent[result.label]\n            assert out.exists() is (mode == \"run\")\n            if mode == \"run\":\n                _assert_archive(out, result.label)\n            continue\n        out = outputs[result.label]\n        others = \", \".join(sorted(name for name in groups[out] if name != result.label))\n        message = f